  "query_preview": "..Strong high pressure will be centered just to our\neast into the middle of next week. This will lead to generally\nabove normal temperatures, with the hottest days forecast today\nand Saturday. Monsoon moisture remains over the region, though PW\nvalues are a bit lower than we saw earlier in the week. There is\nstill plenty of moisture for scattered high country storms and\nisolated activity at lower elevations today. Starting Saturday and\ncontinuing into early next week, additional moisture will arrive\nfrom southeast to northwest with increasing storm coverage, first\nalong the rim and White Mtns Saturday and then spreading farther \nnorth and west each day. Again the main threat with storms will be\nelevated risk for locally heavy rainfall and flash flooding,\nespecially since many areas have wet ground conditions. The\nExtreme Heat Warning continues for the lower elevations of Grand\nCanyon as well as Marble/Glen Canyons through Sunday. Lower\nelevation areas of Yavapai County will also see elevated HeatRisk,\nbut the uncertainty of afternoon storms and associated rain-\ncooled air kept us from issuing a warning there. Temperatures next\nweek should be a bit cooler, but areas that don't see as much\nstorm activity will still be quite hot as the ridge will continue\nto be stronger than usual for late July.",
